<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/17th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Revolt</p><h1 class="enc-title">Leisler's Rebellion</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1689–1691</span> · <a href="/centuries/17th-century">17th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Leisler's Rebellion was an uprising in colonial <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/new-york">New York</a> from 1689 to 1691, after news of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/glorious-revolution">Glorious Revolution</a> and the collapse of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dominion">Dominion</a> of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/new-england">New England</a>. The German-born merchant and militia captain Jacob Leisler seized control of the colony in the name of William and Mary and governed it for nearly two years. When a royal governor arrived in 1691, Leisler was tried for treason and executed.</p></div>
